Here’s the full one-pass hashmap solution:

```python
from typing import List

class Solution:
    def twoSum(self, nums: List[int], target: int) -> List[int]:
        seen = {}

        for i, num in enumerate(nums):
            complement = target - num
            if complement in seen:
                return [seen[complement], i]

            seen[num] = i
```

`seen` remembers each number’s index. For each `num`, the code checks whether its needed partner—the complement—has already appeared. It checks before saving the current number, so an element can’t pair with itself.

